the as of style still works in marieupol  has become a symbol of ukrainian  resistance  in a network of underground bunkers  civilians and ukrainian soldiers have  been trapped for months as russian  forces close in  hundreds of people have been evacuated  from mariupol including some from inside  the plant  but some civilians and soldiers have  refused or been unable to leave in the  last stand for the steel works  is of huge strategic importance the  southern port city is just over 30 miles  from the border with russia  right in the city centre lies the vast  as of stall steel and ironworks it's a  total maze of warehouses and industrial  facilities and the ukrainians have  defended it from the beginning initially  the russian advance was held back to the  city's outskirts but as the war's gone  on russian forces have closed in  by late april the azov style plant was  the only part of mariupol not in russian  hands  and by may russian forces had cut off  the steel works entirely and begun its  bombardment in earnest  but the site has been the target of air  strikes and shelling since the very  start of the conflict  this footage shows a ukrainian tank  outside one of the main entrances on the  first day of the war  the area now is almost completely  unrecognizable  and while the site was under bombardment  in the tunnels and shelters beneath  civilians were hiding  most of the information coming out of  the plant initially came from ukrainian  sources this footage is said to have  been filmed on march 24th  but by mid-april units allied with  russia began releasing footage from  around the industrial complex  this propaganda video from the donetsk  people's republic's telegram channel  shows them firing in the direction of  the plant  inside the aztel bunkers civilians were  still hiding  the same woman we saw in a video from  march appears again in this clip from  april 23rd  by the time this clip was filmed it  appears she'd been living underground  for at least a month  a bloody standoff between russian and  ukrainian troops was looming  extraction  but on the 21st of april russian  president vladimir putin cancelled any  assault  asking instead for the site to be  completely blockaded  it was after this that the united  nations stepped in to help those still  stuck inside  working with russia they escorted over  100 civilians to the town of zaparisha  and charities like the red cross also  helped with the evacuations  [Music]  but russian airstrikes continued to  pound the complex  and reports of a renewed russian ground  assault on the site surfaced from  ukrainian  officials ukrainian forces however  remain defiant  this video appears to show some singing  patriotic songs at night at the steel  plant  sky news hasn't independently verified  when it was filmed  the battle for mariupol has become one  of the defining tragedies of the  ukrainian war and this sprawling  industrial site has been the last pocket  of resistance  there are heavy bloody battles i am  proud of my soldiers for making inhuman  efforts to contain the enemies onslaught  i thank the whole world for the  tremendous support of the mario pole  garrison  our soldiers deserve it  the situation is extremely difficult but  we continue to carry out the order to  keep the defense despite everything
 

